#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Setup {#setup}"
msgstr "Setup {#setup}"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"
msgstr "Maliit na halimbawa ng simulator {#small-scale-simulator-example}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before submitting a hardware job, we validate the entire workflow on a local"
" noisy simulator. We use `AerSimulator.from_backend(backend)` to build a "
"simulator that inherits the noise model and coupling map of the backend you "
"selected, so the simulator response is qualitatively similar to what we "
"expect from hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bago magsumite ng hardware job, ina-validate natin ang buong workflow sa "
"isang lokal na maingay na simulator. Ginagamit natin ang "
"`AerSimulator.from_backend(backend)` upang bumuo ng simulator na nagmamana "
"ng noise model at coupling map ng backend na iyong pinili, kaya ang tugon ng"
" simulator ay kalidad na katulad ng inaasahan natin mula sa hardware.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-"
"inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr ""
"Hakbang 1: I-map ang mga classical input sa isang quantum problem "
"{#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We write the CHSH circuit with a single parameter $\\theta$, which sweeps "
"the measurement basis of the first qubit. The "
"[`Estimator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-"
"runtime/estimator-v2) primitive simplifies the analysis: it returns "
"expectation values of observables directly, and it can evaluate a "
"parameterized circuit at many parameter values in a single call.\n"
msgstr ""
"Isinusulat natin ang CHSH Circuit na may isang parameter na $\\theta$, na "
"nag-i-sweep ng measurement basis ng unang qubit. Pinasimple ng "
"[`Estimator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-"
"runtime/estimator-v2) primitive ang pagsusuri: direkta nitong ibinabalik ang"
" mga expectation values ng mga observable, at kaya nitong suriin ang isang "
"parameterized circuit sa maraming parameter values sa isang tawag.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/chsh-"
"inequality/extracted-outputs/c3f57d25-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/chsh-"
"inequality/extracted-outputs/c3f57d25-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, we create a list of 21 phase values from $0$ to $2\\pi$ at which to "
"evaluate the parameterized circuit ($0$, $0.1\\pi$, $0.2\\pi$, ..., "
"$1.9\\pi$, $2\\pi$).\n"
msgstr ""
"Susunod, gagawa tayo ng listahan ng 21 phase values mula $0$ hanggang "
"$2\\pi$ kung saan susuriin ang parameterized circuit ($0$, $0.1\\pi$, "
"$0.2\\pi$, ..., $1.9\\pi$, $2\\pi$).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally we define the observables. The first qubit is measured along axes "
"rotated by $\\theta$; the second qubit is measured in $Z$ and $X$. With "
"those choices, the four CHSH correlators map to the Pauli operators $ZZ$, "
"$ZX$, $XZ$, and $XX$:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa wakas, tinutukoy natin ang mga observable. Ang unang qubit ay sinusukat "
"sa mga axes na inikot ng $\\theta$; ang pangalawang qubit ay sinusukat sa "
"$Z$ at $X$. Sa mga pagpipiliang ito, ang apat na CHSH correlators ay "
"namamapa sa mga Pauli operator na $ZZ$, $ZX$, $XZ$, at $XX$:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle S_1 \\rangle = \\langle ZZ \\rangle - \\langle ZX \\rangle + \\langle XZ \\rangle + \\langle XX \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle S_1 \\rangle = \\langle ZZ \\rangle - \\langle ZX \\rangle + \\langle XZ \\rangle + \\langle XX \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle S_2 \\rangle = \\langle ZZ \\rangle + \\langle ZX \\rangle - \\langle XZ \\rangle + \\langle XX \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle S_2 \\rangle = \\langle ZZ \\rangle + \\langle ZX \\rangle - \\langle XZ \\rangle + \\langle XX \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-"
"problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr ""
"Hakbang 2: I-optimize ang problema para sa quantum hardware execution "
"{#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"V2 primitives only accept circuits and observables that conform to the "
"instructions and connectivity supported by the target system (instruction "
"set architecture, or ISA, circuits and observables). We build the "
"`AerSimulator` from the backend and transpile against the simulator's target"
" so the same pass manager is exercised end-to-end.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga V2 primitive ay tumatanggap lamang ng mga circuit at observable na "
"sumusunod sa mga instruction at connectivity na sinusuportahan ng target "
"system (instruction set architecture, o ISA, circuits at observables). "
"Binubuo natin ang `AerSimulator` mula sa backend at ini-transpile gamit ang "
"target ng simulator upang ang parehong pass manager ay magamit mula simula "
"hanggang dulo.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/chsh-"
"inequality/extracted-outputs/3e139a89-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/chsh-"
"inequality/extracted-outputs/3e139a89-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We also transform the observables to match the transpiled circuit's qubit "
"layout using `SparsePauliOp.apply_layout`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Binabago rin natin ang mga observable upang tumugma sa qubit layout ng "
"transpiled circuit gamit ang `SparsePauliOp.apply_layout`.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-"
"primitives}"
msgstr ""
"Hakbang 3: Isagawa gamit ang mga Qiskit primitive {#step-3-execute-using-"
"qiskit-primitives}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Run the parameter sweep with `EstimatorV2` in `aer_sim` mode. The Estimator "
"`run()` method takes an iterable of PUBs. Each PUB has the format `(circuit,"
" observables, parameter_values, precision)`. We pass both observables "
"together so they share the same parameter sweep.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pinapatakbo ang parameter sweep gamit ang `EstimatorV2` sa `aer_sim` mode. "
"Ang `run()` method ng Estimator ay tumatanggap ng isang iterable ng mga PUB."
" Ang bawat PUB ay may format na `(circuit, observables, parameter_values, "
"precision)`. Ipinapasa natin ang parehong observable nang magkasama upang "
"maibahagi nila ang parehong parameter sweep.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format "
"{#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr ""
"Hakbang 4: I-post-process at ibalik ang resulta sa nais na classical format "
"{#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Estimator returns expectation values for both observables. We plot them "
"against $\\theta$ together with the classical bound ($\\pm 2$) and the "
"Tsirelson bound ($\\pm 2\\sqrt{2}$). The shaded grey regions mark the gap "
"between the two. Points that lie inside these bands violate the CHSH "
"inequality.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ibinabalik ng Estimator ang mga expectation values para sa parehong "
"observable. Ini-plot natin ang mga ito laban sa $\\theta$ kasama ang "
"classical bound ($\\pm 2$) at ang Tsirelson bound ($\\pm 2\\sqrt{2}$). Ang "
"mga shaded grey na lugar ay nagmamarka ng agwat sa pagitan ng dalawa. Ang "
"mga puntong nasa loob ng mga band na ito ay lumalabag sa CHSH inequality.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/chsh-"
"inequality/extracted-outputs/c8fd5140-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/chsh-"
"inequality/extracted-outputs/c8fd5140-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The simulator's CHSH witnesses already exceed the classical bound of $\\pm "
"2$ at several values of $\\theta$, even with the backend's noise model. The "
"peaks fall just short of the Tsirelson bound $\\pm 2\\sqrt{2}$ because of "
"simulated device noise. With the workflow validated, we move on to actual "
"hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga CHSH witness ng simulator ay lumampas na sa classical bound na $\\pm"
" 2$ sa ilang mga value ng $\\theta$, kahit na may noise model ng backend. "
"Ang mga tuktok ay bahagyang kulang sa Tsirelson bound na $\\pm 2\\sqrt{2}$ "
"dahil sa simulate na device noise. Sa na-validate na workflow, magpatuloy na"
" tayo sa tunay na hardware.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Large-scale hardware example {#large-scale-hardware-example}"
msgstr ""
"Malaking-sukat na halimbawa ng hardware {#large-scale-hardware-example}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A CHSH test is intrinsically a *two-qubit* experiment, so it does not scale "
"by making one circuit bigger. Instead, it scales by running **many tests in "
"parallel**. Here we tile the backend with as many disjoint Bell pairs as its"
" connectivity allows (a *matching* of the coupling map) and run an "
"independent CHSH sub-circuit on every pair, all in a single job.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang CHSH test ay mahalagang isang *two-qubit* na eksperimento, kaya hindi "
"ito lumalaki sa pamamagitan ng paggawa ng mas malaking Circuit. Sa halip, "
"lumalaki ito sa pamamagitan ng pagpapatakbo ng **maraming test nang sabay-"
"sabay**. Dito natin binabalot ang backend ng kasindaming disjoint Bell pair "
"hangga't pinapayagan ng connectivity nito (isang *matching* ng coupling map)"
" at nagpapatakbo ng independiyenteng CHSH sub-circuit sa bawat pair, lahat "
"sa isang job.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This turns CHSH into a **device-wide benchmark of entanglement quality**: "
"rather than a single hand-picked pair, we test entanglement across a large "
"fraction of the chip at once, under realistic conditions where every pair "
"contends with its neighbors' crosstalk and parallel-gate errors. Violating "
"the inequality on every pair *simultaneously* certifies that genuine "
"entanglement is available everywhere on the device.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ginagawa nitong isang **device-wide benchmark ng kalidad ng entanglement** "
"ang CHSH: sa halip na isang hand-picked na pair, sinusubukan natin ang "
"entanglement sa malaking bahagi ng chip nang sabay-sabay, sa makatotohanang "
"kondisyon kung saan ang bawat pair ay nakikipaglaban sa crosstalk ng mga "
"kapitbahay at mga parallel-gate error. Ang paglabag sa inequality sa bawat "
"pair *sabay-sabay* ay nagpapatunay na ang tunay na entanglement ay available"
" sa lahat ng dako ng device.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/chsh-"
"inequality/extracted-outputs/3376bc73-1.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/chsh-"
"inequality/extracted-outputs/3376bc73-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The faint curves are the individual Bell pairs and the bold curves are their"
" mean across the device. Every pair traces the same sinusoid predicted by "
"quantum mechanics, and the spread between the faint curves reflects the "
"variation in noise from pair to pair. Wherever a curve enters the grey "
"bands, it has crossed the classical bound of $\\pm 2$, and the printed "
"summary confirms that essentially every pair violates the CHSH inequality at"
" the same time.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga maputlang kurba ay ang mga indibidwal na Bell pair at ang mga "
"makapal na kurba ay ang kanilang average sa buong device. Bawat pair ay "
"sumusubaybay sa parehong sinusoid na hinuhulaan ng quantum mechanics, at ang"
" pagkalat sa pagitan ng mga maputlang kurba ay sumasalamin sa pagkakaiba-iba"
" ng noise mula sa pair hanggang sa pair. Saan man pumapasok ang isang kurba "
"sa mga grey band, lumampas na ito sa classical bound na $\\pm 2$, at ang "
"naka-print na buod ay nagpapatunay na halos bawat pair ay lumalabag sa CHSH "
"inequality nang sabay-sabay.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The peaks fall short of the Tsirelson bound $\\pm 2\\sqrt{2}$ because of "
"device noise, but the conclusion is unambiguous: the backend sustains "
"genuine entanglement across the whole chip simultaneously, not just on a "
"single hand-picked pair. This is the sense in which the CHSH experiment "
"\"scales\": not as one larger circuit, but as a parallel benchmark that "
"certifies entanglement everywhere at once.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga tuktok ay kulang sa Tsirelson bound na $\\pm 2\\sqrt{2}$ dahil sa "
"device noise, ngunit ang konklusyon ay malinaw: ang backend ay nagpapanatili"
" ng tunay na entanglement sa buong chip nang sabay-sabay, hindi lamang sa "
"isang hand-picked na pair. Ito ang kahulugan kung saan \"lumalaki\" ang CHSH"
" experiment: hindi bilang isang mas malaking Circuit, kundi bilang isang "
"parallel benchmark na nagpapatunay ng entanglement sa lahat ng dako nang "
"sabay-sabay.\n"

